The new candidate chain is:

    atomic complete-train mass <= (2f-k)/D
      -> 2f-k >= 2*sqrt(pi/(2*sqrt(3)))*D-o(D)
      -> 4(q-k)-k-2z >= (2*pi+2*sqrt(pi/(2*sqrt(3))))*D-o(D)
      -> (q-k)/D >= 2.0469527302-o(1)
      -> the entire Type-II (q-k)/D <= 1.860 branch is empty.

It also gives f/D >= sqrt(pi/(2*sqrt(3)))-o(1). The high-(q-k)/D
Type-II branch and the macroscopic-container branch remain open.
The source retains every contact isolate through the imported canonical
premises. Neither graph counting nor the face floor supplies a motion,
a uniform face-width bound, or a full Level I contradiction.

