## Finite reciprocal cut bank and literal contact returns

Run base c2856c7b, theorem state Audit.134. Canonical new inputs:
C-RECIPROCAL-TRAIN-GRAPH, C-AUGMENTED-TRAIN-RANK, and Theory 01
Theorems 10.6/10.8. The exact quantity attacked is the distinct train
bank reaching an outer chain through the complementary train system.

For any chosen complete train family A, let N be its complement and
I the bounded-face recipients in N components missing the outer walk.
Reciprocal sparsity gives E(I)<=2|I|-sigma; terminal counting gives
the cut X(I)>=Q(I)+2sigma. Hence at least |A|/3 distinct A trains
have an end in a boundary-reaching N component.

Matched unit-edge endpoints along each N train form a literal contact
rail of d_tau edges. Adding the actual facial walks and old outer walk
lifts every counted return into the source contact graph.
The common carrier has at most sum_N d_tau+2T edges.

Selecting A by d_tau>=L avoids all weak direction-measure assumptions.
Mantel gives bank_count>=(2/3)*sqrt([R4-L*T]_+).
For every quadratic-core sequence, fixed epsilon gives a linear bank
of macroscopic long trains with actual loaded returns in a carrier of
epsilon*D^2+O(D) edges. In Type II its bank coefficient approaches
0.6348752045. Taking epsilon to zero slowly gives an o(D^2) carrier
and diverging train lengths, without a uniform macroscopic length floor.

Classification: proved candidate awaiting independent audit/promotion;
registry unreviewed and canonical=false. This finite source extraction
stops at literal contact returns: routes can overlap, and neither
shared-path payment nor a feasible full-source motion is proved.
The subquadratic-core container branch also remains.

