## Train-rich shared-carrier regression

Run base 09d1665e, canonical inputs compared on Audit.137 at 0ce9dc0a.
The proposed implication under test was a small shared physical carrier
plus positive pinned rigidity implying many disjoint returns within the
same small edge budget. This implication is false for artificial pins.

An exact rational two-grain family has 2*m*(m-1) strict unit rhombi,
only O(m) summed rhombus area excess, strictly positive equilibrium at
every free point, and an explicit full-rank pinned contact minor.
The complementary singleton trains and facial walks give a carrier
with 8*m edges. For m/3+O(1) central long-train terminals its disjoint
return capacity is two, while the full graph has one independent
return per chosen terminal, requiring Omega(m^2) total unit steps.

Every source is explicitly nonglobal: a square-grid crop of the same
cardinality has strictly smaller diameter. The specified 6*m pins
are not the actual loaded set; the tested fixtures have only two
actual diameter endpoints. The family also lacks canonical global
roundness. This regression does not refute canonical loaded-return
bounds or the candidate bank/long-terminal separator theorem.

Classification: regression awaiting independent audit, registry
unreviewed and canonical=false. No theorem-state promotion.
